-- title:
--   A q-sandwich bound for prime Hecke elements
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is not properly contained in any submodule with these four properties. Write $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ generated by the tensors $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele that is integral at every height-one prime. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $m$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $m\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. Let $q$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $n_0$ be a unit lying in `primeHeckeSet` $\Lambda_1\,q$, that is: $n_0\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, $q\cdot n_0^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, $n_0^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ and $q^{-1}\cdot n_0\notin\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. Assume further $m^{-1}(n_0m)\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. Then $q\cdot\big((n_0m)^{-1}m\big)\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$.
--
--   This is the integrality half of the two-sided $q$-sandwich $q\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}$-inclusions attached to a prime Hecke element $n_0$ at $q$ conjugated by a connecting idele $m$: since $(n_0m)^{-1}m=m^{-1}n_0^{-1}m$, the assertion is that $m^{-1}(q\,n_0^{-1})m$ is integral. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm), where the degeneracy maps on class sets are matched with the Hecke action at $q$.
